From: bundle15 (Mercury lane 15) — managed typed structural gate for packaged model blobs (corrected)
Subject: [PATCH] Home: managed in-process GGUF structural gate on packaged model evidence

Replaces the previously-rejected Python3-subprocess structural gate with a managed typed
verification seam. It performs a bounded, in-process GGUF scan (magic, version, alignment,
metadata scalar widths, tensor-table bounds, known-extent truncation checks, per-tensor
offset alignment, and supported quantized-block row divisibility) — no external process, no
interpreter, no network, no unshipped Python prerequisite at native eligibility/startup.

This is a SUPPLEMENTARY patch for root-owned files; the bundle lane does not apply it. Run
`git apply --check` with this file. It targets current root source in /workspace/9to1-chat-cui.

WHAT IT DOES
- Adds IHomeDulcheModelStructuralGate + HomeDulchePackagedModelStructuralGate (new file
  HomeDulcheModelStructuralGate.cs in Source/Home/Core, auto-included by the existing
  Source\Home\Core\*.cs compile glob). It passes only on PROVABLE structural soundness and
  fails CLOSED on defect/absence/cancellation. Tensor types outside the supported subset are
  passed through (never bricked, never claimed complete), so the narrow checker does not
  silently block all otherwise-supported bundled/local models.
- Wires the gate into HomeDulchePackagedModelEvidenceSource.VerifyBlobAsync: a model is
  eligible ONLY after real size+hash verification AND structural admission. Cancellation
  propagates (OperationCanceledException) and always fails closed.
- Adds focused owning test regressions: malformed blob, missing artifact, cancellation,
  truncated GGUFv3 (dataStart) rejection vs valid 68-byte counterpart admission, alignment
  type/power-of-two negatives, misaligned tensor offset, zero-dimension, skip-beyond-EOF
  metadata, rollback/previous-known-good, and real source identity. The canonical caller test
  is labelled EVIDENCE-ONLY (it exercises FindEligibleAsync, not
  OverlayChatSessionFactory/provider/broker/model adapter); real caller/inference/asset
  acceptance remains BLOCKED.

CORRECTIONS over the prior reviewer-flagged patch
- declaredExtents now uses consistent unsigned (ulong+ulong) extent math; no ulong+long mix.
- ReadString's nullable result is retained (`string? key`) with explicit null rejection before use.
- The Assert.ThrowsAnyAsync<OperationCanceledException> callback adapts the returned ValueTask
  with .AsTask().
- relative.Replace char literals are valid C# '\\'.
- dataStart is aligned from the reader position AFTER all tensor-info records, not the pre-table
  start; a blob ending exactly at tensor-info end (57 bytes) with no aligned payload is rejected,
  while the padded 68-byte valid counterpart is admitted.
- general.alignment must be a UINT32 scalar with a positive power-of-two bounded value; wrong
  scalar/string type or value 3 is rejected.
- Per-tensor offsets must be aligned; impossible zero dimensions reject; metadata values
  running beyond EOF reject.
- Cancellation token is polled during metadata/tensor scans and before admission; cancelled gates
  propagate OperationCanceledException and never partially admit. No timeout is claimed (the
  verifier is a bounded in-process scan that honours caller cancellation).

Packaging/installer note: no Python artifact is installed or invoked at native runtime; the
Python bundle structural_validate.py remains QA/pack tooling only. The managed gate ships as
compiled assembly code, so there is no unshipped interpreter prerequisite.

SDK/native status: NO SDK/.NET/restore/build/native execution was allocated for this lane.
Compile correctness is delivered by construction (fixed defect lines, validated emitted source
bytes) but remains NOT RUN until the coordinator allocates a Home compile/test slot.

